Note that the openfoam.org (Foundation) and openfoam.com (ESI/OpenCFD) releases
are separate lineages. This case is a Foundation case: it runs through foamRun
with the multicomponentFluid solver module and will not run on an ESI build.


Local deviations from the upstream tutorial
-------------------------------------------
1. constant/thermophysicalTransport  -- ADDED, not shipped by the tutorial.
   Selects the FickianFourier laminar thermophysical transport model with
   mixtureDiffusionCoefficients and a per-specie Dm table. This model is the
   reason the test exists: it has caused trouble for a user before, so
   checks/openfoam/counterflowflame.py asserts the solver actually selects it
   rather than silently falling back to another transport model.

2. system/decomposeParDict           -- ADDED, not shipped by this tutorial.
   scotch decomposition. numberOfSubdomains is rewritten at run time by the
   ReFrame test with foamDictionary to match the job's rank count.

3. system/blockMeshDict              -- MODIFIED.
   The hardcoded block resolution (100 40 1) was replaced with top-level `nx`
   and `ny` entries referenced as ($nx $ny 1), so the test can scale the mesh
   with foamDictionary. The defaults still reproduce the tutorial's 4000 cells.

4. system/controlDict                -- MODIFIED.
   writeInterval raised from 0.05 to 0.5 (= endTime) so the case writes once at
   the end instead of ten times. Write frequency does not affect the solution,
   but on a scaled-up mesh ten writes would put the shared filesystem, rather
   than the solver, into the measurement.

Everything under 0/ and the remaining constant/ files are byte-for-byte the
upstream tutorial files. When updating, re-copy from upstream and re-apply the
four deviations above rather than hand-editing.
